# A single triangle with a Blinn-Phong material, used by MaterialTests.
#
# **It exists because an OBJ cannot say how rough a surface is.** Model I/O returns a roughness of
# 0.9 for every OBJ material whatever the file contains — `Ns`, `Pr` and `Pm` alike — so the specular
# exponent is the only shininess the format actually carries through.
mtllib box-exponent.mtl
v 0 0 0
v 1 0 0
v 0 1 0
vt 0 0
vt 1 0
vt 0 1
vn 0 0 1
usemtl glossy
f 1/1/1 2/2/1 3/3/1
